<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-INTERVIEW-Command sees takeover reward.</title>
<headline>RTRS-INTERVIEW-Command sees takeover reward.</headline>
<byline>James Regan</byline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>An agreed takeover bid launched on Wednesday for Command Petroleum Ltd by United Kingdom-based Cairn Energy Plc would reward shareholders who stuck with Command's shares when they had little market recognition or value, Command managing director John Doran said.</p>
<p>&quot;Those shareholders that have followed the stock over four years from 14 cents to A$1.10, they should be allowed an opportunity to monetise,&quot; Doran told Reuters in an interview.</p>
<p>Command shares last traded at 97 cents on September 24 before being voluntarily suspended pending merger talks.</p>
</text>
